lenovo-yoga-c940-14iil (1.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * support: battery conservation mode on by default (TLP
    STOP_CHARGE_THRESH_BAT0/BAT1=1 for the ideapad battery plugin); holds the
    charge at about 55-60%. The earlier "does not keep it" finding was an
    immediate read-back: the firmware applies the write after about 3 s.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0800

lenovo-yoga-c940-14iil (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * windows-vm: no longer Depends on util-linux (Essential; lintian
    depends-on-essential-package-without-using-version), description lines
    wrapped, manual page yoga-windows-vm(1) added.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0800

lenovo-yoga-c940-14iil (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New binary package lenovo-yoga-c940-14iil-windows-vm: the existing Windows
    install in a KVM virtual machine (overlay mode by default, raw mode behind
    an explicit switch, autostart off by default).

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0700

lenovo-yoga-c940-14iil (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: depends on convertible-helper, convertible-power and
    grub-large-console, on the Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, SOF audio and Intel graphics
    firmware packages and on iio-sensor-proxy, and installs this laptop's TLP
    settings.  Includes a feature check script.  The fingerprint reader
    (06cb:00be) is unsupported by libfprint and is not made to work.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:30:00 -0700
